<title>UK: David Brown plans 75 mln-100 mln U.S. buy-FT.</title>
<headline>David Brown plans 75 mln-100 mln U.S. buy-FT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK industrial gears and pumps maker David Brown Plc plans to make a 75-100 million stg buy in the U.S., the Financial Times reported.</p>
<p>The newspaper said that the company has hired Gleacher NatWest to seek purchase candidates and that Chris Cook, David Brown's chairman, flew to the U.S. on Sunday for meetings with potential targets.</p>
<p>The FT said that David Brown is ready to undertake a share issue to finance any deal.</p>
<p>No one could be reached at the company to comment on the report.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom 44 171 542 5887</p>
</text>
